72e;color:#adbac7; overflow-x: auto;" tabindex=3D"0" data-language=3D"bash"=
><code><span class=3D"line"><span style=3D"color:#F69D50">sudo</span><span =
style=3D"color:#96D0FF"> airodump-ng</span><span style=3D"color:#96D0FF"> m=
on0</span><span style=3D"color:#6CB6FF"> --band</span><span style=3D"color:=
#96D0FF"> abg</span><span style=3D"color:#6CB6FF"> -w</span><span style=3D"=
color:#96D0FF"> capture_file</span><span style=3D"color:#6CB6FF"> --output-=
format</span><span style=3D"color:#96D0FF"> pcap</span></span></code><butto=
n class=3D"copy-code-btn">Copy</button></pre>
<h3 id=3D"windows">Windows<a href=3D"https://sageaxe.com/blog/wireshark-wif=
i-packet-capture#windows" class=3D"heading-anchor" aria-label=3D"Copy link =
to this section"><svg width=3D"15" height=3D"15" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" fill=
=3D"none" stroke=3D"currentColor" stroke-width=3D"2" stroke-linecap=3D"roun=
d" stroke-linejoin=3D"round" aria-hidden=3D"true"><path d=3D"M10 13a5 5 0 0=
07.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 00-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"></path><path d=3D"M14 11a5 5 0 =
00-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 007.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"></path></svg></a></h3>
<p>Windows has historically been the most challenging platform for monitor =
mode. The standard NDIS driver model does not expose a monitor mode API to =
user-space applications. Three approaches are available [Wireshark Wiki, =
=E2=80=9CWLAN (IEEE 802.11) Capture Setup=E2=80=9D]:</p>
<p><strong>Npcap with Monitor Mode</strong>: Npcap (the successor to WinPca=
p) supports monitor mode on some adapters. Install Npcap with the =E2=80=9C=
Support raw 802.11 traffic=E2=80=9D option enabled. In Wireshark, select th=
e Wi-Fi adapter and check the monitor mode checkbox in Capture Options. Thi=
s works with adapters that have Npcap-compatible drivers, but support varie=
s widely.</p>
<p><strong>Microsoft Network Monitor / Message Analyzer</strong>: Microsoft=
=E2=80=99s now-deprecated Network Monitor 3.x could capture in monitor mode=
 using the built-in Windows driver. While no longer actively developed, it =
remains functional on Windows 10 and earlier.</p>
<p><strong>Dedicated Capture Adapters</strong>: The most reliable approach =
on Windows is a dedicated USB Wi-Fi adapter with a chipset known to support=
 monitor mode under Npcap. The Mediatek MT7612U and Realtek RTL8812AU chips=
ets have reasonable support. The Netgear A6210 (MT7612U) is commonly used f=
or this purpose.</p>
<h2 id=3D"wireshark-column-configuration-for-wireless">Wireshark Column Con=
figuration for Wireless<a href=3D"https://sageaxe.com/blog/wireshark-wifi-p=
acket-capture#wireshark-column-configuration-for-wireless" class=3D"heading=
-anchor" aria-label=3D"Copy link to this section"><svg width=3D"15" height=
=3D"15" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" fill=3D"none" stroke=3D"currentColor" stroke-=
width=3D"2" stroke-linecap=3D"round" stroke-linejoin=3D"round" aria-hidden=
=3D"true"><path d=3D"M10 13a5 5 0 007.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 00-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.=
71"></path><path d=3D"M14 11a5 5 0 00-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 007.07 7.07l1.71-=
1.71"></path></svg></a></h2>
<p>The default Wireshark column layout is designed for wired Ethernet. For =
wireless troubleshooting, a customized column set dramatically improves rea=
dability. The following columns are essential for 802.11 analysis [Wireshar=
k User=E2=80=99s Guide, =E2=80=9CCustomizing the Packet List=E2=80=9D]:</p>






































































<table><thead><tr><th>Column Title</th><th>Field</th><th>Purpose</th></tr><=
/thead><tbody><tr><td>Time</td><td>frame.time_relative</td><td>Time since c=
apture start</td></tr><tr><td>Channel</td><td>wlan_radio.channel</td><td>Ch=
annel the frame was captured on</td></tr><tr><td>Signal (dBm)</td><td>wlan_=
radio.signal_dbm</td><td>RSSI of the received frame</td></tr><tr><td>Data R=
ate</td><td>wlan_radio.data_rate</td><td>PHY data rate in Mbps</td></tr><tr=
><td>Type/Subtype</td><td>wlan.fc.type_subtype</td><td>Frame type (beacon, =
probe, data, etc.)</td></tr><tr><td>Source</td><td>wlan.sa</td><td>Source M=
AC address</td></tr><tr><td>Destination</td><td>wlan.da</td><td>Destination=
 MAC address</td></tr><tr><td>BSSID</td><td>wlan.bssid</td><td>BSS identifi=
er</td></tr><tr><td>SSID</td><td>wlan.ssid</td><td>Network name (from beaco=
ns/probes)</td></tr><tr><td>Duration</td><td>wlan.duration</td><td>NAV dura=
tion in microseconds</td></tr><tr><td>Retry</td><td>wlan.fc.retry</td><td>W=
hether this is a retransmission</td></tr><tr><td>Info</td><td>info</td><td>=
Wireshark=E2=80=99s auto-generated summary</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>To add these columns: right-click the column header bar, select Column P=
references, and add each field. You can also apply a column by right-clicki=
ng a field in the packet detail pane and selecting =E2=80=9CApply as Column=
.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p>The <strong>Signal</strong> and <strong>Data Rate</strong> columns depen=
d on the radiotap or PPI header that the capture adapter prepends to each f=
rame. Not all adapters provide all radiotap fields. The signal strength fie=
ld is particularly valuable =E2=80=94 it tells you the RSSI at which the ca=
pturing adapter received the frame, which indicates proximity and link qual=
ity [IEEE 802.11-2020, Section 11.11].</p>
<h2 id=3D"capture-filters">Capture Filters<a href=3D"https://sageaxe.com/bl=
og/wireshark-wifi-packet-capture#capture-filters" class=3D"heading-anchor" =
aria-label=3D"Copy link to this section"><svg width=3D"15" height=3D"15" vi=
ewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" fill=3D"none" stroke=3D"currentColor" stroke-width=3D"2=
" stroke-linecap=3D"round" stroke-linejoin=3D"round" aria-hidden=3D"true"><=
path d=3D"M10 13a5 5 0 007.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 00-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"></path>=
<path d=3D"M14 11a5 5 0 00-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 007.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"></pat=
h></svg></a></h2>
<p>Capture filters (BPF syntax) reduce the volume of data written to disk d=
uring capture. They operate at the driver level and are applied before Wire=
shark processes the frames. This matters during high-density captures where=
 millions of frames per minute are common [Wireshark User=E2=80=99s Guide, =
=E2=80=9CCapture Filters=E2=80=9D].</p>
<p><strong>Capture only management frames</strong> (type 0):</p>
<pre class=3D"astro-code github-dark-dimmed" style=3D"background-color:#222=
72e;color:#adbac7; overflow-x: auto;" tabindex=3D"0" data-language=3D"plain=
text"><code><span class=3D"line"><span>wlan type mgt</span></span></code><b=
utton class=3D"copy-code-btn">Copy</button></pre>
<p><strong>Capture only frames from a specific BSSID</strong>:</p>
<pre class=3D"astro-code github-dark-dimmed" style=3D"background-color:#222=
72e;color:#adbac7; overflow-x: auto;" tabindex=3D"0" data-language=3D"plain=
text"><code><span class=3D"line"><span>wlan host aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff</span></=
span></code><button class=3D"copy-code-btn">Copy</button></pre>
<p><strong>Capture only probe requests and probe responses</strong>:</p>
<pre class=3D"astro-code github-dark-dimmed" style=3D"background-color:#222=
72e;color:#adbac7; overflow-x: auto;" tabindex=3D"0" data-language=3D"plain=
text"><code><span class=3D"line"><span>wlan type mgt subtype probe-req or w=
lan type mgt subtype probe-resp</span></span></code><button class=3D"copy-c=
ode-btn">Copy</button></pre>
<p><strong>Capture only data frames</strong> (type 2):</p>
<pre class=3D"astro-code github-dark-dimmed" style=3D"background-color:#222=
72e;color:#adbac7; overflow-x: auto;" tabindex=3D"0" data-language=3D"plain=
text"><code><span class=3D"line"><span>wlan type data</span></span></code><=
button class=3D"copy-code-btn">Copy</button></pre>
<p><strong>Capture on a specific channel</strong> (requires setting the cha=
nnel on the adapter separately =E2=80=94 BPF cannot filter by channel):</p>
<pre class=3D"astro-code github-dark-dimmed" style=3D"background-color:#222=
72e;color:#adbac7; overflow-x: auto;" tabindex=3D"0" data-language=3D"plain=
text"><code><span class=3D"line"><span># Set channel first:</span></span>
<span class=3D"line"><span>sudo iw dev mon0 set channel 149 HT80</span></sp=
an>
<span class=3D"line"><span># Then capture all frames on that channel</span>=
</span></code><button class=3D"copy-code-btn">Copy</button></pre>
<h2 id=3D"display-filters">Display Filters<a href=3D"https://sageaxe.com/bl=
og/wireshark-wifi-packet-capture#display-filters" class=3D"heading-anchor" =
aria-label=3D"Copy link to this section"><svg width=3D"15" height=3D"15" vi=
ewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" fill=3D"none" stroke=3D"currentColor" stroke-width=3D"2=
" stroke-linecap=3D"round" stroke-linejoin=3D"round" aria-hidden=3D"true"><=
path d=3D"M10 13a5 5 0 007.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 00-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"></path>=
<path d=3D"M14 11a5 5 0 00-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 007.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"></pat=
h></svg></a></h2>
<p>Display filters operate on the already-captured data and support the ful=
l Wireshark display filter syntax. These are more expressive than capture f=
ilters and can reference any field in the protocol dissector [Wireshark Use=
r=E2=80=99s Guide, =E2=80=9CBuilding Display Filter Expressions=E2=80=9D].<=
/p>
<h3 id=3D"association-and-authentication-analysis">Association and Authenti=
cation Analysis<a href=3D"https://sageaxe.com/blog/wireshark-wifi-packet-ca=
pture#association-and-authentication-analysis" class=3D"heading-anchor" ari=
a-label=3D"Copy link to this section"><svg width=3D"15" height=3D"15" viewB=
ox=3D"0 0 24 24" fill=3D"none" stroke=3D"currentColor" stroke-width=3D"2" s=
troke-linecap=3D"round" stroke-linejoin=3D"round" aria-hidden=3D"true"><pat=
h d=3D"M10 13a5 5 0 007.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 00-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"></path><pa=
th d=3D"M14 11a5 5 0 00-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 007.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"></path><=
/svg></a></h3>
<p><strong>All management frames</strong>:</p>
<pre class=3D"astro-code github-dark-dimmed" style=3D"background-color:#222=
72e;color:#adbac7; overflow-x: auto;" tabindex=3D"0" data-language=3D"plain=
text"><code><span class=3D"line"><span>wlan.fc.type =3D=3D 0</span></span><=
/code><button class=3D"copy-code-btn">Copy</button></pre>
<p><strong>Beacon frames only</strong> (what each AP advertises: SSID, supp=
orted rates, RSN and capability elements):</p>
<pre class=3D"astro-code github-dark-dimmed" style=3D"background-color:#222=
72e;color:#adbac7; overflow-x: auto;" tabindex=3D"0" data-language=3D"plain=
text"><code><span class=3D"line"><span>wlan.fc.type_subtype =3D=3D 0x08</sp=
an></span></code><button class=3D"copy-code-btn">Copy</button></pre>
<p><strong>Filter by SSID</strong> (the SSID is carried only in beacons, pr=
obe requests/responses and association requests, so this matches those fram=
es, not every frame of the network):</p>
<pre class=3D"astro-code github-dark-dimmed" style=3D"background-color:#222=
72e;color:#adbac7; overflow-x: auto;" tabindex=3D"0" data-language=3D"plain=
text"><code><span class=3D"line"><span>wlan.ssid =3D=3D "CorpWiFi"</span></=
span></code><button class=3D"copy-code-btn">Copy</button></pre>
<p>To see every frame of one network, filter on its BSSID instead (<code>wl=
an.bssid =3D=3D aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff</code>); find the BSSID from the beacon t=
hat matched the SSID filter.</p>
<p><strong>Probe requests from a specific client</strong>:</p>
<pre class=3D"astro-code github-dark-dimmed" style=3D"background-color:#222=
72e;color:#adbac7; overflow-x: auto;" tabindex=3D"0" data-language=3D"plain=
text"><code><span class=3D"line"><span>wlan.fc.type_subtype =3D=3D 0x04 &am=
p;&amp; wlan.sa =3D=3D aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff</span></span></code><button class=
=3D"copy-code-btn">Copy</button></pre>
<p><strong>Authentication frames (both open system and SAE)</strong>:</p>
<pre class=3D"astro-code github-dark-dimmed" style=3D"background-color:#222=
72e;color:#adbac7; overflow-x: auto;" tabindex=3D"0" data-language=3D"plain=
text"><code><span class=3D"line"><span>wlan.fc.type_subtype =3D=3D 0x0b</sp=
an></span></code><button class=3D"copy-code-btn">Copy</button></pre>
<p><strong>Association requests and responses</strong>:</p>
<pre class=3D"astro-code github-dark-dimmed" style=3D"background-color:#222=
72e;color:#adbac7; overflow-x: auto;" tabindex=3D"0" data-language=3D"plain=
text"><code><span class=3D"line"><span>wlan.fc.type_subtype =3D=3D 0x00 || =
wlan.fc.type_subtype =3D=3D 0x01</span></span></code><button class=3D"copy-=
code-btn">Copy</button></pre>
<p><strong>Deauthentication and disassociation frames</strong>:</p>
<pre class=3D"astro-code github-dark-dimmed" style=3D"background-color:#222=
72e;color:#adbac7; overflow-x: auto;" tabindex=3D"0" data-language=3D"plain=
text"><code><span class=3D"line"><span>wlan.fc.type_subtype =3D=3D 0x0c || =
wlan.fc.type_subtype =3D=3D 0x0a</span></span></code><button class=3D"copy-=
code-btn">Copy</button></pre>
<p><strong>Deauth with a specific reason code</strong> (e.g., reason 7 =3D =
Class 3 frame from non-associated station):</p>
<pre class=3D"astro-code github-dark-dimmed" style=3D"background-color:#222=
72e;color:#adbac7; overflow-x: auto;" tabindex=3D"0" data-language=3D"plain=
text"><code><span class=3D"line"><span>wlan.fc.type_subtype =3D=3D 0x0c &am=
p;&amp; wlan.fixed.reason_code =3D=3D 7</span></span></code><button class=
=3D"copy-code-btn">Copy</button></pre>
<h3 id=3D"data-frame-analysis">Data Frame Analysis<a href=3D"https://sageax=
e.com/blog/wireshark-wifi-packet-capture#data-frame-analysis" class=3D"head=
ing-anchor" aria-label=3D"Copy link to this section"><svg width=3D"15" heig=
ht=3D"15" viewBox=3D"0 0 24 24" fill=3D"none" stroke=3D"currentColor" strok=
e-width=3D"2" stroke-linecap=3D"round" stroke-linejoin=3D"round" aria-hidde=
n=3D"true"><path d=3D"M10 13a5 5 0 007.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 00-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1=
.71"></path><path d=3D"M14 11a5 5 0 00-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 007.07 7.07l1.71=
-1.71"></path></svg></a></h3>
<p><strong>All data frames from a specific client</strong>:</p>
<pre class=3D"astro-code github-dark-dimmed" style=3D"background-color:#222=
72e;color:#adbac7; overflow-x: auto;" tabindex=3D"0" data-language=3D"plain=
text"><code><span class=3D"line"><span>wlan.fc.type =3D=3D 2 &amp;&amp; wla=
n.sa =3D=3D aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff</span></span></code><button class=3D"copy-cod=
e-btn">Copy</button></pre>
<p><strong>Retransmitted frames only</strong> (high retransmission rates in=
dicate RF issues):</p>
<pre class=3D"astro-code github-dark-dimmed" style=3D"background-color:#222=
72e;color:#adbac7; overflow-x: auto;" tabindex=3D"0" data-language=3D"plain=
text"><code><span class=3D"line"><span>wlan.fc.retry =3D=3D 1</span></span>=
</code><button class=3D"copy-code-btn">Copy</button></pre>
<p><strong>QoS data frames with a specific TID</strong> (e.g., TID 6 =3D Vo=
ice):</p>
<pre class=3D"astro-code github-dark-dimmed" style=3D"background-color:#222=
72e;color:#adbac7; overflow-x: auto;" tabindex=3D"0" data-language=3D"plain=
text"><code><span class=3D"line"><span>wlan.fc.type_subtype =3D=3D 0x28 &am=
p;&amp; wlan.qos.tid =3D=3D 6</span></span></code><button class=3D"copy-cod=
e-btn">Copy</button></pre>
